file=Comms & PR/signal/logical/book-requirements.md · h=<!--\nLogical layer: touch-1 placeholder per §8.1.\n\nPer §8.1: leave a placeholder — record the specific 0.6-flagged judgments this agent\nmakes, what kind of book/source would ground each, and why. Do not build real logical\nartifacts early.\n\nPer §8.7: this is the ONLY .md file in an agent's logical/ folder.\n\nPer §8.11: includes 5 required tables + Cross-Agent Book Coordination.\n\nsignal has 0 local Python utilities (all 3 skills Route D — cited rubrics + templates).\nNo graduation-to-Shared OS/logical/ path for scripts; only cited-rubric assets in Touch-2.\n-->\n · p:=Records the §0.6-flagged judgments signal's 3 skills make today, describes what\nbook / source type would ground each, and lists candidate authenticated sources per §8.8\nfor a future Touch-2 build. **No real logical scripts have been built for signal yet.**\nsignal has 0 local Python utilities (all 3 skills Route D). Every judgment is currently\nflagged reasoning-based or Tier-B book-cited. Touch-2 runs when books are placed in\n`Agents/_books/`.\n\nCross-agent note: **McCord 2018** (already grounding hire identity + several P&C skills)\n+ **Scott 2020** (already grounding herald identity + 4 herald artifacts) BOTH continue\nto serve signal via tone inheritance from herald. Same books, no additional placement\nneeded for tone-side. Signal-specific books (Kotter + Bridges + Prosci + Heath brothers\n+ Minto) are net-new for the Comms & PR fleet.\n\n · st(:Scripts Table (built for signal in Shared OS/logical/)=Per §8.11 required table shape:\n · tb=\| Script filename \| Source book(s) \| Book URL(s) \| Route \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| _(none)_ \| _(none)_ \| _(none)_ \| _(none)_ \| · st(:Scripts Table (built for signal in Shared OS/logical/)=**Current count: 0.** signal has 0 local Python utilities — all 3 skills are Route D\n(cited rubrics + template libraries). Touch-2 will produce Route-D cited-rubric assets\nin Shared OS/logical/ but no Python scripts.\n\n · tb=\| Script filename \| Source book(s) \| Book URL(s) \| Why signal needs it \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| _(none)_ \| _(none)_ \| _(none)_ \| _(none)_ \| · is:Table (from Shared OS/logical/)=**Current count: 0.** No relevant Shared OS/logical/ scripts exist yet for signal to\ninherit.\n\n · sm:=Per §8.11:\n · tb=\| Skill \| Shared OS/logical/ imports today \| Rationale \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| internal-comms (marketplace) \| _(none)_ \| Anthropic-official marketplace skill; content verbatim per §4.8; no signal-specific script imports \| · tb=\| internal-cadence \| _(none)_ \| Awaiting `Shared OS/logical/internal_cadence.md` (Route D asset) — see Still Pending §1 \| · tb=\| change-comms \| _(none)_ \| Awaiting `Shared OS/logical/change_comms.md` (Route D asset) — see Still Pending §2 \| · sm:=**Current count: 0 imports.**\n\n · tb=\| §0.6-flagged judgment \| Clearing script/asset \| Tier before \| Tier after \| Cleared? \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| _(no flags cleared yet)_ \| — \| — \| — \| ❌ \| · fc:Summary=**Cleared: 0 of 11 flags.** See Still Pending below.\n\n · sp:Still Pending=The 11 §0.6-flagged judgments across signal's 3 skills, grouped by the future Shared OS\nasset that would ground each.\n · ### §1. `Shared OS/logical/internal_cadence.md` — Route D cited rubric (would ground `internal-cadence`)=**Flags this asset would clear:**\n · tb=\| # \| Flag \| Skill line \| Current tier \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| 1 \| Channel-cadence matrix (7 message types → channel + cadence + optional format-routing) \| internal-cadence § Structure/Protocol §1; § Instructions Phase 1 (LOAD-BEARING) \| Tier B (practitioner-institutional discipline — Fournier + Google re:Work cited but not book-page-cited from `Agents/_books/`) \| · tb=\| 2 \| Decision broadcast 3-part structure (WHAT / WHY / WHAT-CHANGES) with honest-WHY discipline \| internal-cadence § Structure/Protocol §3; § Principles rules 2 + 3 (LOAD-BEARING) \| Tier B (Minto Pyramid Principle + McCord inherited via herald identity; canonical but not page-cited) \| · tb=\| 3 \| All-hands 4-artifact discipline (prepared doc 24-48hr advance + live 60-90 min + Q&A live+async + async recording+summary 24hr) \| internal-cadence § Structure/Protocol §4; § Instructions Phase 4; § Principles rule 4 (LOAD-BEARING) \| Tier C reasoning-based (practitioner heuristic; specific timing thresholds not book-cited) \| · tb=\| 4 \| Searchable archive discipline (permanent link + tags + cross-refs + never-silent-contradiction) \| internal-cadence § Structure/Protocol §5; § Instructions Phase 5; § Principles rule 6 (LOAD-BEARING) \| Tier C reasoning-based (practitioner discipline; not book-cited) \| · tb=\| 5 \| Close-the-loop discipline (visible action from previous cycle before next) \| internal-cadence § Principles rule 5 (LOAD-BEARING); § Instructions Phase 6 \| Tier B (Udext research + inherited from maslow's pulse-survey minimum-viable-action) \| · ### §1. `Shared OS/logical/internal_cadence.md` — Route D cited rubric (would ground `internal-cadence`)=**Candidate authenticated sources per §8.0 + §8.8:**\n\n- **Heath, Chip & Heath, Dan (2007).** *Made to Stick: Why Some Ideas Survive and Others Die.* Random House. ISBN 978-1400064281. SUCCESS framework for memorable decision broadcasts. Named practitioner-authors per §8.9.\n- URL: publisher; PAYWALL.\n- **Minto, Barbara (1996).** *The Pyramid Principle: Logic in Writing and Thinking.* Prentice Hall. ISBN 978-0273710516. Structured-writing discipline for decision broadcasts. Named academic-practitioner.\n- URL: publisher; PAYWALL.\n- **Scott, Kim (2017).** *Radical Candor.* SHARED — already cited across P&C + Comms & PR identity work (herald identity + P&C precedent). §8.9 extract-once-use-many.\n- URL: Scott author site; PAYWALL.\n- **Fournier, Camille (2017).** *The Manager's Path.* O'Reilly. ISBN 978-1491973899. Practitioner reference for internal-comms cadence in engineering-adjacent orgs.\n- URL: O'Reilly publisher; PAYWALL.\n- **Udext + Gallup** (institutional practitioner) — pulse-survey research already cited in maslow. §8.9 extract-once-use-many.\n\n**Route:** Route D (cited rubric — framework + template library, no formula, no script).\n\n · ### §2. `Shared OS/logical/change_comms.md` — Route D cited rubric (would ground `change-comms`)=**Flags this asset would clear:**\n · tb=\| # \| Flag \| Skill line \| Current tier \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| 6 \| Kotter's 8-step change model (Create urgency → Build coalition → Form vision → Enlist volunteers → Enable action → Generate short-term wins → Sustain acceleration → Institute change) \| change-comms § Structure/Protocol; § Instructions Phase 4 + 7 \| Tier B (Kotter 1996/2012 canonical academic per §8.8 — HBS professor emeritus; cited but not book-page-cited from `Agents/_books/`) \| · tb=\| 7 \| Bridges' Transition Model (Ending / Neutral Zone / New Beginning) + Neutral Zone highest-leverage phase \| change-comms § Structure/Protocol; § Instructions Phase 6; § Principles rule 4 (LOAD-BEARING) \| Tier B (Bridges 1991/2009 canonical practitioner-academic; cited but not book-page-cited) \| · tb=\| 8 \| Prosci ADKAR (Awareness / Desire / Knowledge / Ability / Reinforcement) individual-change methodology \| change-comms § Structure/Protocol; § Instructions Phase 7 \| Tier B (Prosci institutional practitioner framework per §8.8; cited but framework-level rather than book-cited) \| · tb=\| 9 \| Legal fence BEFORE change-comms drafting (employment counsel + WARN Act + protected-class + severance + international) \| change-comms § Instructions Phase 2; § Principles rule 1 (LOAD-BEARING) \| Tier B (Universal Principle 5 legal fence + Rothstein et al. Employment Law casebook candidate — same book candidate as hire's worker_classification.py per §8.9) \| · tb=\| 10 \| Audience segmentation (6 standard segments — affected / directly-affected / retained / adjacent / customers-partners / board-investors) \| change-comms § Instructions Phase 3; § Principles rule 2 (LOAD-BEARING) \| Tier C reasoning-based (practitioner heuristic; not book-cited) \| · tb=\| 11 \| Reinforcement window (6-26 weeks; institutional anchoring + ADKAR reinforcement + short-term wins) \| change-comms § Instructions Phase 7; § Principles rule 5 (LOAD-BEARING) \| Tier C reasoning-based (Kotter step 8 timing heuristic; not book-cited specifically) \| · ### §2. `Shared OS/logical/change_comms.md` — Route D cited rubric (would ground `change-comms`)=**Candidate authenticated sources per §8.0 + §8.8:**\n\n- **Kotter, John P. (1996, updated 2012).** *Leading Change.* Harvard Business School Press. ISBN 978-1422186435. Named academic per §8.8 (HBS professor emeritus). Foundational 8-step change model.\n- URL: publisher; PAYWALL. Grounds §6 directly.\n- **Bridges, William & Susan (1991, 3rd ed 2009).** *Managing Transitions: Making the Most of Change.* Da Capo Lifelong Books. ISBN 978-0738213804. Practitioner-academic reference. Transition Model (Ending / Neutral Zone / New Beginning) — the LOAD-BEARING Neutral Zone framing.\n- URL: publisher; PAYWALL. Grounds §7 directly — HIGH-PRIORITY given Neutral Zone LOAD-BEARING status.\n- **Prosci ADKAR institutional materials** — Jeffrey Hiatt / Prosci Learning Center. Institutional practitioner framework per §8.8.\n- URL: https://www.prosci.com/methodology/adkar — some materials FREE.\n- **McCord, Patty (2018).** *Powerful.* SHARED — already cited across P&C identity (hire) + Comms & PR identity (herald via Scott inheritance). Direct-honest layoff-comms voice.\n- URL: Silicon Guild publisher; PAYWALL.\n- **Rothstein, M. A., Craver, C. B., Schroeder, E. P., & Shoben, E. W. (multiple editions).** *Employment Law* casebook. SHARED with hire's `worker_classification.py` + grove's `training_ops.py` per §8.9.\n- URL: Foundation Press / West Academic Publishing; PAYWALL.\n\n**Route:** Route D (cited rubric — framework layered on framework, no formula, no script).\n\n**HIGH-PRIORITY Touch-2 candidate:** Bridges 2009 — grounds Neutral Zone LOAD-BEARING rule\n(Principle 5 across signal + Universal Principle 5). Without Bridges, the "why Neutral\nZone matters" case rests on Tier B framework-cited without book-page grounding.\n\n · bsp:Book Sourcing Plan Summary=Per §8.11 litmus ("Can the operator click one link and see the actual book page?"):\n · tb=\| Book \| Free? \| URL \| Blocking asset \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Kotter (1996, updated 2012), *Leading Change* \| PAYWALL \| Harvard Business School Press publisher \| `change_comms.md` §6 (Kotter 8-step foundational) \| · tb=\| **Bridges (1991, 3rd ed 2009), *Managing Transitions*** \| PAYWALL \| Da Capo Lifelong publisher \| `change_comms.md` §7 (Neutral Zone LOAD-BEARING framing — HIGHEST-PRIORITY signal-specific) \| · tb=\| **Prosci ADKAR institutional materials** \| **Partial FREE** \| https://www.prosci.com/methodology/adkar \| `change_comms.md` §8 (partial free-buildable) \| · tb=\| McCord (2018), *Powerful* \| PAYWALL \| Silicon Guild publisher \| `change_comms.md` §9 (direct-honest layoff voice) — **SHARED with hire identity + P&C precedent per §8.9** \| · tb=\| Rothstein et al., *Employment Law* casebook \| PAYWALL \| Foundation Press / West Academic \| `change_comms.md` §9 legal-fence — **SHARED with hire's worker_classification.py + grove's training_ops.py per §8.9** \| · tb=\| Heath brothers (2007), *Made to Stick* \| PAYWALL \| Random House publisher \| `internal_cadence.md` §2-3 (decision broadcast + SUCCESS framework) \| · tb=\| Minto (1996), *The Pyramid Principle* \| PAYWALL \| Prentice Hall publisher \| `internal_cadence.md` §2 (structured-writing discipline) \| · tb=\| Scott (2017), *Radical Candor* \| PAYWALL \| Scott author site \| `internal_cadence.md` § voice inheritance — **SHARED with herald identity + P&C precedent** \| · tb=\| Fournier (2017), *The Manager's Path* \| PAYWALL \| O'Reilly publisher \| `internal_cadence.md` supplementary \| · tb=\| **Udext + Gallup** (institutional) \| Partial FREE \| https://www.udext.com/blog + https://www.gallup.com \| `internal_cadence.md` §5 close-loop discipline — **SHARED with maslow's motivation-map** \| · bsp:Book Sourcing Plan Summary=**Recommendation for the operator per §8.8b decision point:**\n\n- **PARTIAL free-only builds possible today:**\n- `change_comms.md` §8 ADKAR grounding partial from FREE Prosci materials\n- `internal_cadence.md` §5 close-loop grounding already partial from FREE Udext/Gallup +\n§8.9 inherited from maslow\n- **HIGHEST-PRIORITY signal-specific Touch-2 candidate:** **Bridges 2009 — Managing\nTransitions**. Grounds the Neutral Zone LOAD-BEARING rule which is signal's most\ndistinctive load-bearing discipline (change-comms Principle 4; Universal Principle 5).\n- **Cross-agent leverage via §8.9 extract-once:**\n- **McCord 2018** — grounds hire identity + Comms & PR change-comms voice; single\nplacement serves 2+ agents (hire + signal via herald tone inheritance).\n- **Scott 2017** — grounds herald identity + signal tone inheritance; single placement\nserves 2 agents (herald + signal).\n- **Rothstein et al. Employment Law casebook** — grounds hire's `worker_classification.py`\n+ grove's `training_ops.py` retention + signal's change-comms legal-fence; single\nplacement serves 3+ agents.\n- **Udext + Gallup** — already grounds maslow's minimum-viable-action rule; signal\ninherits.\n- **Full Touch-2 requires operator to place 4-5 paywalled books in `Agents/_books/`:**\nKotter 2012 (change_comms §6); Bridges 2009 (change_comms §7 HIGHEST-PRIORITY);\nHeath brothers 2007 (internal_cadence §2-3); Minto 1996 (internal_cadence §2).\n- **Route-D-only fallback:** signal keeps its 3 Route-D skills as agent-local; §0.6\nflags stay Tier B or Tier C (framework-cited but not book-page-cited). Load-bearing\nrules remain enforced structurally at config + tool-permissions level regardless of\nbook placement (same pattern as herald's AVE refusal being enforced without book\nplacement).\n\nThe operator picks the path per §8.8b when Touch-2 opens.\n\n · tb=\| Book \| Grounds for signal \| Grounds for other agents \| Coordination note \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| **McCord (2018), *Powerful*** \| `change_comms.md` §9 direct-honest layoff-comms voice \| hire identity (Patty McCord anchor) + P&C precedent \| Already-placed shared book across 3+ agents. Signal inherits via herald tone inheritance. \| · tb=\| **Scott (2017), *Radical Candor*** \| `internal_cadence.md` voice inheritance + solicit-first discipline \| herald identity + several herald skills + P&C precedent \| Already-placed shared book across 4+ agents. Signal inherits via herald tone inheritance. \| · tb=\| **Rothstein et al., *Employment Law* casebook** \| `change_comms.md` §9 legal-fence grounding \| hire's `worker_classification.py` + grove's `training_ops.py` retention \| **THREE-WAY SHARED** — single placement serves hire + grove + signal per §8.9. \| · tb=\| **Udext + Gallup** \| `internal_cadence.md` §5 close-loop discipline \| maslow's `motivation-map` minimum-viable-action rule \| Already-institutional shared source; single reference serves 2+ agents. \| · tb=\| **Kotter (1996, 2012), *Leading Change*** \| `change_comms.md` §6 Kotter 8-step \| No other current agent uses Kotter; potentially future Growth & Partnerships (change-management-adjacent for market entry) \| Signal-specific for now. \| · tb=\| **Bridges (1991, 2009), *Managing Transitions*** \| `change_comms.md` §7 Neutral Zone LOAD-BEARING framing \| No other current agent uses Bridges \| Signal-specific; HIGHEST-PRIORITY signal-Touch-2 candidate. \| · tb=\| **Prosci ADKAR** \| `change_comms.md` §8 ADKAR individual-change methodology \| No other current agent uses Prosci \| Signal-specific; PARTIAL FREE via Prosci institutional materials. \| · tb=\| **Heath brothers (2007), *Made to Stick*** \| `internal_cadence.md` §2-3 SUCCESS framework for memorable comms \| No other current agent uses Heath brothers \| Signal-specific. \| · tb=\| **Minto (1996), *The Pyramid Principle*** \| `internal_cadence.md` §2 structured-writing discipline \| Potentially future Executive Office / echo for pitch materials \| Signal-specific for now; potential future cross with echo. \| · tb=\| **Fournier (2017), *The Manager's Path*** \| `internal_cadence.md` supplementary practitioner reference \| Potentially future Engineering / dev-adjacent skills for engineering-leader comms cadence \| Signal-specific for now. \| · m:Meta=- **Touch-1 built:** 2026-07-31.\n- **Touch-2 status:** waiting on book placement in `Agents/_books/`. Signal-specific books\nKotter 2012, Bridges 2009, Prosci (partial FREE), Heath brothers 2007, Minto 1996 are\nall net-new to the Comms & PR + P&C fleet. Cross-agent-shared books (McCord, Scott,\nRothstein, Udext+Gallup) already have precedent.\n- **HIGHEST-PRIORITY signal-Touch-2 candidate: Bridges 2009 — Managing Transitions.**\nGrounds the Neutral Zone LOAD-BEARING rule which is signal's most distinctive\nload-bearing discipline (change-comms Principle 4).\n- **Structural enforcement independent of book placement:** signal's 9 LOAD-BEARING\nREFUSALS at tool-permissions level (legal-fence + skip-Neutral-Zone + corporate-\neuphemism + silent-contradiction + material-NPI + external-facing + individual-perf-data\n+ segmented-below-min-group + fabricate) are enforced STRUCTURALLY regardless of book\nplacement. Same pattern as herald's AVE refusal being code-level enforced without book\nplacement. Book placement further-strengthens academic case but doesn't change runtime\nbehavior.\n- **Refresh trigger:** any new skill added to signal, any change to a skill's Principles\nsection introducing a new numeric/heuristic judgment, or completion of a Touch-2 book\ncampaign.\n